= Internet protocol suite — Simple =

The Internet protocol suite is the family of interoperating protocols used to communicate across the Internet, commonly organized into link, Internet, transport, and application layers.

The suite includes IP for network-layer packet delivery, transport protocols such as TCP and UDP, and many application protocols such as HTTP and DNS-related protocols.

'''Important boundaries:'''
* Internet protocol suite ≠ Internet itself
* TCP/IP ≠ TCP and IP only

